# This CITATION.cff describes the normet R package. Keep the version, title and
# abstract in step with DESCRIPTION when they change.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "normet: Normalisation, Decomposition, and Counterfactual Modelling for Air Quality Time-Series"
version: 1.0.1
abstract: >-
  Provides a suite of tools for advanced air quality time series analysis.
  Core functionalities include meteorological normalisation (de-weathering)
  to reveal underlying trends in data like air pollution concentrations,
  and causal inference using both classic and machine learning-based
  Synthetic Control Methods (SCM). The package features high-level workflows
  for uncertainty quantification, time-series decomposition, and robust
  placebo tests, powered by H2O AutoML or lightgbm backends.
authors:
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: Congbo
    email: congbo.song@manchester.ac.uk
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7948-4834"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/apai-sys/normet-r"
url: "https://github.com/apai-sys/normet-r"
